// =====================================================================
// examdata.js  -  仮免許学科試験 模擬問題 (Provisional License Written Test)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5 sets (Q1 ~ Q4, R1) x 50 questions each = 250 questions total.
//
// Each question object:
//   q           : the statement shown to the learner (正/誤 question)
//   answer      : '正' (the statement is correct) or '誤' (it is wrong)
//   explanation : why the answer is 正 / 誤 (Japanese)
//   myanmar     : short Burmese explanation (for Myanmar learners)
//
// Optional furigana column (hiragana printed above the kanji in the question):
//   furigana    : annotated copy of `q` using {base|れあでぃんg} marks, e.g.
//                 'この標識は{止まれ|とまれ}を示す。'
//                 Each {…|…} becomes <ruby>base<rt>reading</rt></ruby>.
//                 Stripping the marks must reproduce `q` exactly -- this is
//                 enforced by validateExamData() below, so `q` itself always
//                 stays plain text (search, grading, photos unaffected).
//
// Optional picture fields (picture + text mixed, like the real exam):
//   img         : image path or URL, e.g. 'img/no-uturn.png'
//   svg         : inline SVG string (same convention as rulesdata.js)
//   caption     : small label drawn under the picture
//   layout      : 'left' (picture beside the text, default) | 'top'
//
//   A picture uploaded from the exam screen (🖼 画像を追加) is stored in
//   Supabase Storage at traffic-photos / exam-photos/<setId>-<number>.jpg
//   and takes priority over img / svg -- so artwork can be attached to any
//   question without editing this file.
//
// Conventions (keep this file diff-friendly and machine-checkable):
//   * one question per line, keys in the order q, furigana (optional),
//     answer, explanation, myanmar
//   * never type the question number into `q`: the UI prints 問N from the
//     array index (script.js > renderExamQuestions) and uploaded pictures are
//     keyed '<setId>-<index>', so a number in the text only duplicates it
//   * Japanese keywords inside `myanmar` go in parentheses, e.g. (徐行)
//   * validateExamData() at the bottom warns in the console if any of this
//     drifts (wrong question count, bad answer value, numbered `q`, ...)
//
// Scoring: 50 questions per set. Same pass rule as the real 仮免学科試験:
//   45 questions or more correct out of 50  =>  合格 (90%)
// =====================================================================

